From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quartz/colour: Output ARGB32.

The Color Space Converter only offered the opaque RGB formats. Native
also converts to MEDIASUBTYPE_ARGB32: an application that asks its
Sample Grabber for ARGB32 frames gets the converter inserted after the
decoder (the WMV decoder DMO offers no ARGB32).

Game impacted: Gunslinger Stratos 2 (Type X3) plays its movies (the
BYKING intro, the attract and tutorial videos) through a Sample Grabber
set to ARGB32 and a Null Renderer, then copies the grabbed buffer to a
Direct3D 11 texture. Connecting the grabber failed (autoplug recursion
depth reached) and the game skipped every movie.

Offer ARGB32 last, after the opaque formats, with its alpha bytes set
to 0xff.
---
--- a/dlls/quartz/colour.c
+++ b/dlls/quartz/colour.c
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@
     {&MEDIASUBTYPE_RGB565, 16, {0xf800, 0x07e0, 0x001f}},
     {&MEDIASUBTYPE_RGB555, 16, {0x7c00, 0x03e0, 0x001f}},
     {&MEDIASUBTYPE_RGB8, 8},
+    /* Last: offered after the opaque formats. Its alpha bytes are set to 0xff. */
+    {&MEDIASUBTYPE_ARGB32, 32},
 };
 
 static DWORD image_size(const BITMAPINFOHEADER *header)
@@ -266,6 +268,12 @@
     }
     GdiFlush();
     memcpy(dst, bits, size);
+    if (IsEqualGUID(&filter->source.pin.mt.subtype, &MEDIASUBTYPE_ARGB32))
+    {
+        DWORD *pixel = (DWORD *)dst, count = size / sizeof(DWORD);
+
+        while (count--) *pixel++ |= 0xff000000;
+    }
     IMediaSample_SetActualDataLength(converted, size);
     IMediaSample_SetSyncPoint(converted, TRUE);
     IMediaSample_SetPreroll(converted, IMediaSample_IsPreroll(sample) == S_OK);
